    "body": "Here's an even more interesting case, to stress test stepping.\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<input type=number id=input min=\"-100000000\" step=\"1e-12\" value=0>\r\n<script>\r\n  const LONG_MAX = 2147483647; // maximum value of long IDL type\r\n  input.stepUp(LONG_MAX);\r\n  console.log(input.value);\r\n</script>\r\n```\r\n\r\nEven though Firefox and Chrome both use some high-precision decimal library, their output is different: Chrome outputs 0, while Firefox outputs 0.002147483647. I checked with jsdom that even if a naïve floating point operation were to be used, it should still be 0.002147483647. Not sure if this is a bug in Chrome or Firefox or jsdom.",
